From 837a8a0ee3a2d6400646eaa691725a26062939c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Murat=20Du=C4=9Fan?=
 <111883464+MuratDugan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:55:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] session: cancel the data hole punch in chiaki_session_stop

With a PSN connection the session thread calls
chiaki_holepunch_session_punch_hole() for the data port while holding
state_mutex. That call waits for the console in three steps of up to
30 seconds each. chiaki_session_stop() starts by locking state_mutex,
so a stop requested in that window does nothing for 30 to 90 seconds,
and the calling thread is stuck for as long.

Cancel the hole punch before taking the lock.
chiaki_holepunch_main_thread_cancel() only takes the holepunch
session's own stop_mutex.

One thing to check when reviewing: if the stop arrives after the hole
punch has finished, main_should_stop can still be set when
chiaki_holepunch_session_fini() waits for the deletion notification,
and that wait would then return CANCELED instead of confirming the
deletion. In my tests (stop during a running stream) the deletion was
still confirmed and logged as usual.
---
 lib/src/session.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/src/session.c b/lib/src/session.c
index 41c6bbf..8397792 100644
--- a/lib/src/session.c
+++ b/lib/src/session.c
@@ -313,6 +313,11 @@ CHIAKI_EXPORT ChiakiErrorCode chiaki_session_start(ChiakiSession *session)
 
 CHIAKI_EXPORT ChiakiErrorCode chiaki_session_stop(ChiakiSession *session)
 {
+	// The session thread keeps state_mutex locked while it punches the hole for the
+	// data connection, which can wait on the console for up to 90 seconds. Cancel
+	// that wait first, otherwise the lock below does not return until it is over.
+	if(session->holepunch_session)
+		chiaki_holepunch_main_thread_cancel(session->holepunch_session, false);
 	ChiakiErrorCode err = chiaki_mutex_lock(&session->state_mutex);
 	assert(err == CHIAKI_ERR_SUCCESS);
 
